---
import type { Chapter } from '../lib/chapters';
import { COMMIT_DATE, COMMIT_SHA } from '../lib/provenance';
import Pill from './Pill.astro';

interface Props {
  chapters: Chapter[];
}
const { chapters } = Astro.props;

const live = chapters.filter((c) => c.data.status === 'live');
const drafting = chapters.filter((c) => c.data.status === 'draft');
const outlined = chapters.filter((c) => c.data.status === 'plan');

const publishedMinutes = live.reduce((sum, c) => sum + c.data.mins, 0);
const hours = Math.floor(publishedMinutes / 60);
const mins = publishedMinutes % 60;
const readingTime = hours > 0 ? `${hours} h ${mins} m` : `${mins} m`;

---

<main class="cover" id="cover">
  <div class="cover-main">
    <p class="eyebrow t-meta">Written in the open · <b>{live.length > 0 ? `Chapter ${live.length} published this week` : 'Drafting'}</b></p>

    <h1 class="t-display">The AI-Native <em>Engineer</em></h1>

    <p class="deck">Software engineering after the typing bottleneck. How specifications, agents and provenance replace the craft assumptions that thirty years of practice were built on.</p>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href={`/${chapters[0]?.id ?? '#'}`}>Start reading <small>· ch. 00</small></a>
      <a class="btn" href="#" download>↓ PDF <small>· 4.2 MB</small></a>
      <a class="btn" href="#" download>↓ EPUB <small>· 1.1 MB</small></a>
    </div>

    <p class="t-meta flush">Free to read online and free to download. No account, no email wall.</p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <div class="meta-panel">
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Edition</span><span class="v">0.0.0 · living draft</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Last commit</span><span class="v">{COMMIT_DATE} · <span class="dot"></span><span class="tabular">{COMMIT_SHA}</span></span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Chapters</span><span class="v">{live.length} published · {drafting.length} drafting · {outlined.length} outlined</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Reading time</span><span class="v">{readingTime} published</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Licence</span><span class="v">CC BY 4.0 + DEL v1.0</span></div>
      <div class="row"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v"><span class="dot"></span>Building in public</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="cover-side">
    <h3>Contents</h3>
    <p>Chapters go live as they are finished. Outlined chapters show their argument so you can see where the book is heading.</p>
    <nav class="cover-index" aria-label="Book contents">
      {chapters.map((c) => (
        <a class="index-row" href={`/${c.id}`}>
          <span class="n">{c.data.n}</span>
          <span class="t">{c.data.title}</span>
          <Pill status={c.data.status} />
        </a>
      ))}
    </nav>

    <h3 class="spaced">The author</h3>
    <p>Kevin Ryan has spent thirty years in enterprise engineering, from CERN to the BBC, the Financial Times and Nestlé. He now runs an AI-native consultancy in Europe.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
